            <profile id="00ca-076c-a0d6-3a07" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="15ea-5299-d0f5-5dbb" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Hand weapon and bow. May choose from the equipment available to Noble Cavalry of the selected tribe (see the army composition notes). Army General. For the Army General in Avar, Later Khazar and Cuman armies exceeding 2,000 pts, the Khagan may be upgraded to Great Khagan (+25 pts, Leadership 10). Begs use the Lesser Khagan entry, Sultans the Khagan entry and Khans the Great Khagan entry (Cumans). 0-1 Army General (with the Lesser Khan). If a Beg (Khagan or Great Khagan) is the Later Khazar Army General he may dismount (-3 pts, reduce Movement to 4) and be fielded in a Beg War Wagon (+55 pts). (Byzantium p.59)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="e09c-e4b8-b78b-15c0" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">None</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
              <modifiers>
                <!-- armour-save -->
