            <profile id="7e6a-1692-d9ec-e4e5" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="15ea-5299-d0f5-5dbb" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Hand weapon and bow. See the Noble Cavalry equipment of the selected tribe (see the army composition notes). The wealthiest and most renowned warriors of any tribe. Light Cavalry (Avar nobles with light armour are Expert Horsemen with Feigned Flight; armoured Avar Nobles with Kontarion and Later Khazar Noble Cavalry with heavy armour, spear and barding or half-barding are Superior Cavalry; Cumans with heavy armour are Expert Horsemen with Feigned Flight). 0-2 units. (Byzantium p.59)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="6ba5-9f23-2adf-7654" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">6+</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
              <modifiers>
                <!-- armour-save -->
