          <profiles>
            <profile id="221b-bb00-9fd9-e234" name="War Wagon" publicationId="15ea-5299-d0f5-5dbb" hidden="false" typeId="a802-40b5-d980-cabc" typeName="Model">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="M" typeId="35a2-714d-db3e-3738">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="WS" typeId="bb04-2b70-ae79-3559">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="BS" typeId="ffff-54f0-d131-b6a9">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="S" typeId="9e7c-6fc0-c50c-ee53">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="T" typeId="d226-f704-80f9-6e23">7</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="W" typeId="ce59-af10-7f37-4238">3</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="I" typeId="8ec4-e9a6-0b8a-08aa">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="A" typeId="ee87-e286-4768-82be">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Ld" typeId="b6d1-0987-3a4d-d6a9">-</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="52a3-fa96-82c6-7d64" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="15ea-5299-d0f5-5dbb" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">The War Wagon may have up to four guards armed with a hand weapon, light armour and a shield at the cost of +8 pts per model. The War Wagon is immobile and counts as a large target, if targeted specifically. Alternatively, the models inside the War Wagon can be targeted - they count as being behind hard cover, and use the wagon as a defended obstacle in close combat. All fleeing Khazar units that come within 6" of the War Wagon may immediately take a Rally test, even if in the middle of a flight. If the test is passed, the unit rallies and may reform. Units that were pursued and caught but who managed to rally do not count as destroyed - the pursuing unit counts as charging in the next turn of close combat. Later Khazars only; Special Units may be either Yurts &amp; Defenders, or the Beg War Wagon. Only if a Beg (Khagan or Great Khagan) is the Army General. (Byzantium p.57)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="55"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
